    "Ongoing investigations involve inquiries into possible political actors, with some observers suggesting links to treason-related activities."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police (Polri) has reassigned three high-ranking generals who were named suspects in an ongoing investigation regarding the alleged illegal wiretapping of President Prabowo Subianto. These officers have been transferred to the Yanma Polri while the legal process continues. The case has garnered significant public and political attention, with various figures speculating about the involvement of intellectual actors or political masterminds behind the breach. Members of the Partai Keadilan Sejahtera (PKS) have formally urged law enforcement to ensure the investigation remains transparent and objective. Additional discussions surrounding the case have touched upon the potential application of the Electronic Information and Transactions (ITE) Law and possible connections to treason investigations. The Police Chief, Listyo Sigit, has been involved in high-level discussions regarding the case as authorities work to mitigate the spread of misinformation related to the wiretapping claims.",
